# Copy to server/.env if you want to override defaults. Never commit the real file.
#
# This app needs NO API keys. Everything runs on free public services:
#   - OpenStreetMap / Nominatim / Photon for maps and geocoding
#   - public search results and business websites for contact discovery
#   - a small offline model for category and location understanding
PORT=5002
SCRAPER_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Desktop-only: refuse scrape requests without a valid licence
# LICENSE_ENFORCE=1
# LICENSE_FILE=%APPDATA%\Scraper\license.json

# ── Sign-in ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default so a local checkout opens straight into the workspace.
# Set AUTH_REQUIRED=1 and VITE_AUTH_REQUIRED=1 together for a public host.
# AUTH_REQUIRED=0
# SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-48-random-bytes
# SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=604800

# Google Sign-In is optional. Create a Web OAuth client, add the app origins,
# then set the client ID here. Without it the login page shows a SETUP chip and
# email + password still works.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=yourcompany.com
# GOOGLE_MASTER_DOMAIN=yourcompany.com
# GOOGLE_AUTO_PROVISION=0

# Provision a user (scrypt hash, data/users.json):
#   node scripts/create-user.js --email you@example.com --password "…" --role master

